- op: update  # 99fc
  at: '2026-05-17T20:28:51Z'  # 99fc
  by: agent  # 99fc
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 99fc
  clock: 8  # 99fc
  nonce: 99fc  # 99fc
  set:  # 99fc
    description: "**REVISED 2026-05-17** (rolls forward the 2026-04-25 revision with three new findings from code-level investigation). The original 2026-04-25 framing said the cross-file `from X import BAR` case was already working and the real gap was intra-file bare-name reads. The 2026-05-17 investigation confirmed both halves AND surfaced three things the 2026-04-25 description didn't fully address:\n\n- The intra-file gap has **two independent gates**, both of which must relax for the fix to work.\n- The \"fold Deliverable A into WI-ramuv when it lands\" sequencing suggestion is **stale** — WI-ramuv shipped (done, PR #3363). Both deliverables are now unblocked.\n- The orphan-variable count has drifted: 1,171 (cited in the original) → **1,301** per `WI-hahor`'s 2026-05-16 round-14 measurement. The fix's expected impact is therefore slightly larger than originally claimed.\n\n## What's already working\n\n- **Cross-file `from X import BAR` for variable Symbols**: the `_extract_import_edges` pass at `packages/hypergumbo-lang-mainstream/src/hypergumbo_lang_mainstream/py.py:1861` already calls `_lookup_symbol_by_module` without a kind filter, finds variable-kind Symbols, and emits an `imports` edge whose `dst` points at the actual variable Symbol id. Verified example: the `imports` edge for `from ir import PASS_VERSION` lands at `dst='python:packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/ir.py:42-42:PASS_VERSION:variable'` — the real Symbol, not a synthesized boundary.\n- The reason it LOOKS like an in-degree of 1 instead of N is Plan A's src-side collapse + tuple-dedup: every importer's `imports` edge has `src=make_file_id(file)` which canonicalises to `python:<external>:0-0:file:file`, then (canonical, BAR, \"imports\") collapses across all importers. **WI-ramuv has now shipped** (done, PR #3363) and restored importer-count attribution; this part of the system is no longer a known gap.\n\n## What is NOT working (the real gap, with the dual-gate finding)\n\n**Intra-file bare-name reads of module-level constants don't emit edges.** The 1,301 orphan `variable` Symbols on hypergumbo self-analysis (per `WI-hahor` 2026-05-16 round 14) are constants that have no cross-file importer at all — they're defined and read entirely WITHIN their own module. Three verified examples:\n\n| Symbol | Defined | Read |\n|---|---|---|\n| `ANDROID_MANIFEST` | `xml_config.py:58` | `xml_config.py:474` (`if path.name == ANDROID_MANIFEST`) |\n| `APEX_BUILTINS` | `apex.py:55` | `apex.py:658, 695` |\n| `PASS_ID` | various | same-file uses inside class methods (e.g. `dependency.py:123, 164`) |\n\n**The cause is two independent gates in `py.py`, both of which need to relax for any fix to work end-to-end:**\n\n**Gate 1 — kind filter at `py.py:2585`:**\n\n```python\ndef _emit_function_ref(name_node: ast.Name, caller: Symbol) -> None:\n    ...\n    if symbol and symbol.kind in (\"function\", \"method\"):  # ← variable kind excluded\n        edges.append(Edge.create(... edge_type=\"references\" ...))\n```\n\nEven when an ast.Name read IS walked, the resolver explicitly drops variable Symbols on the floor.\n\n**Gate 2 — syntactic-context filter in `process_code_block` at `py.py:2680-2708`:**\n\n`_emit_function_ref` is invoked only in 5 specific contexts: assignment RHS, call positional args, call keyword args, dict values, and list/tuple elements. It is NOT invoked for ast.Name reads inside `Compare`, `BinOp`, `If` conditions, return statements, or attribute receivers. The `ANDROID_MANIFEST` read sits inside `ast.Compare` and is invisible to the current walk.\n\n**Implication for fix design:** Deliverable A (relax the kind gate alone) would not actually move the orphan-variable metric because Gate 2 still suppresses the relevant call sites. The fix has to address both gates.\n\n## Two distinct deliverables (recommend rolling A into B's PR)\n\n### Deliverable A — semantic refinement (~2 hr, near-zero metric impact alone)\n\nRelax the kind gate at `py.py:2585` to additionally include `variable`-kind Symbols (with `evidence_type='variable_reference'` to distinguish from the existing `function_reference`). Captures the semantic intent — `from X import BAR` where BAR is data is not the same as `from X import func` where func is callable. Won't move the orphan-rate metric in isolation because Gate 2 still suppresses the relevant call sites. **Recommended: fold this single-line change into Deliverable B's PR rather than ship it standalone.** (Earlier description said \"fold into WI-ramuv when it lands\"; WI-ramuv has now landed.)\n\n### Deliverable B — intra-file reference resolution (~half day, real metric impact)\n\nExtend `process_code_block` in `py.py` to walk function and method bodies for `ast.Name` reads beyond the current 5 syntactic contexts. For each name read:\n\n1. Check if the name resolves to a module-level constant defined in the same file (build a per-file constant table at extraction time, keyed by name).\n2. If so, emit a `references` edge from the enclosing function/method Symbol (or the module Symbol, for module-level reads) to the variable Symbol with `evidence_type='ast_name_read'` and `confidence=0.85`.\n\n**Implementation cautions surfaced by code review:**\n\n- **Avoid double emission with the existing 5 call sites.** The generic walk should skip ast.Name positions already handled by `_emit_function_ref` (assignment RHS, call args, dict values, list/tuple elements) when the resolved Symbol is a function/method (those still get the existing `function_reference` edge). For variable-kind reads in those same contexts, emit `variable_reference` per Deliverable A.\n- **Skip function-local shadows.** A function parameter or local assignment named `PASS_ID` shadows the module constant — should NOT emit. Resolve against the per-file constant table only AFTER checking that no enclosing scope rebinds the name.\n- **Module-level reads.** `process_code_block` is invoked at both module level and function-body level. Module-level reads would emit `module_symbol → variable` edges. Defensible (it's still an inbound edge that satisfies `WI-hahor`'s orphan-triage), but call it out in the PR description.\n- **Edge-type taxonomy note.** `references` is already overloaded — `function_reference` for callable-in-non-call-context and now `variable_reference` for constant reads. Both share the same `edge_type='references'`; consumers distinguish via the `evidence_type` meta key. This matches the codebase pattern from ADR-0023 (axis distinctions live in meta, not in edge type).\n\n**Acceptance criteria:**\n- Self-analysis dogfood: orphan `variable` Symbol count drops from ~1,301 to near zero (modulo genuinely export-only constants like `ANALYZER_MODULES` re-exported via `__all__` with no intra-file reader).\n- Overall orphan rate returns toward the v2.5.1 ~1.0% baseline (within ~0.5pp).\n- Cross-file imports continue to work (regression guard).\n- No edge-count explosion: walk is bounded, function-local shadows correctly skip, double emission with existing call sites avoided.\n\n## Sequencing\n\nBoth deliverables are now unblocked (WI-ramuv shipped). Roll Deliverable A's one-line kind-gate relaxation into Deliverable B's PR so the change ships as one coherent unit.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Star-imports (`from X import *`) — separate (and harder) problem.\n- Cross-language constant references — Python-only for this item.\n- Bare-attribute reads of OTHER modules' constants (`other_module.CONSTANT`) — currently handled by `_emit_module_attr_refs` at `py.py:2595`, which emits `module_attr_ref` edges (NOT `references`). Generalising it to ALSO emit `references` for variable Symbols would be a separate enhancement; out of scope here.\n- Promoting \"used by N readers\" into the centrality ranking weighting — a separate enrichment item once the references edges exist.\n- Function-local name resolution beyond the module scope.\n\n## Validation\n\nRun hypergumbo on itself before/after the Deliverable B change. The orphan-rate metric is the primary signal:\n- pre-fix: ~4.9% (1,441 orphans / 29,280 nodes), **1,301** variable orphans (per WI-hahor 2026-05-16)\n- target: ~1.0% (matching 2026-04-05 baseline before WI-gafog)\n\nTag `awaits_bakeoff_validation` at merge time. Claim: \"Python intra-file constant-read resolution emits ~5,000+ new `references` edges on the bakeoff corpus and reduces orphan-variable count by ~95%.\"\n\n## Related items\n\n- `WI-gafog` (done, P2) — predecessor: module-level NAME assignments now indexed as Symbols.\n- `WI-ramuv` (done, P3, PR #3363) — predecessor: file-symbol post-processing canonicalised so importer-count attribution is restored.\n- `WI-hahor` (todo_soft, P3) — **this item is `isbefore WI-hahor`**: orphan-triage of 113 functions + 13 classes + 1,301 variables needs this item's variable-side fix to land first to isolate genuinely-dead-code from analyzer-blindness.\n- `WI-luvig` (todo_hard, P4, under META `INV-zadum`) — loose coupling: if canonical_name were populated for variable Symbols (write-side identity work), the per-file constant table in Deliverable B could key by canonical_name for more reliable resolution. Not a blocker; coordinate if both items get worked together."  # 99fc
